# eval_watcher GPU test (Colab), branch g9-eval-watcher at dc45483 09-evaluation: score the dry run 1 checkpoint (--team5-run), re-pin to p1536 (week 3, task 1)
# env: Linux-6.6.159+-x86_64-with-glibc2.39, python 3.13.16, torch 2.14.1+cu130, Tesla T4, lm_eval 0.4.13, datasets 5.1.0, tokenizers 0.23.3
# Run on a Tesla T4: no native bf16, so the scorer ran fp32 ("lm-eval (Tesla T4, fp32)" below). The lab eval slot
# runs bf16 on a GPU with native bf16, so these times are an upper bound for it.
# The store is a Team 5 LanguageModel at the dry run 1 shape (exp2_muon, T2, 237M parameters) saved through Team 7's
# Checkpointer by tests/make_lab_store.py, a few AdamW steps from random: the scores are chance, as expected.
# "lag after commit" counts from the store's commit time, minutes before these runs; it is not a watcher delay here.

# 1. A Team 5 LanguageModel at the dry run 1 shape (exp2_muon, T2), frozen p1536, 3 commits

$ python teams/09-evaluation/harness_lab/tests/make_lab_store.py --arm teams/05-architecture/configs/arms/exp2_muon.yaml --tokenizer <p1536>/tokenizer.json --tokenizer-sha256 e6b93a93a60520d7b1af2e9242485f443b5596a1e116b8f8798d83bbad25a64b --byte-table teams/04-ke2/results/tables/p1536-s0/raw_table_P32.npz --final --out <lab>/t2
